text I recall the old man's words as I hold on to Nagisa's hand.
text None of it made a lick of sense to me.
text The old man's story seemed incomprehensible.
text But one vague point did make its way across.
text And it was the same as the pain that I had always felt inside of my chest.
text This town keeps changing.
text And that big wave of change engulfs us... driving us apart.
text An unstoppable force will steal Nagisa away from me.
text Some day...
text Some day, even these hands of ours will have to let go of each other.
text I don't want to think about that day.
text That all-too-painful day.
text Nagisa...
text You'll always be by my side, right...?
text Together with our child... who you'll be bringing into this world...
